  body: "# Missing evidence for an Income Support element\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor IS, the
    captured passage permits an applicable amount to be awarded without housing costs or the severe disability
    premium where evidence is insufficient, and describes revision or supersession when further information
    arrives.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is expressly the IS procedure in DMG 23029–23030. It does
    not authorise applying the same procedure to JSA, refusing an entire claim automatically, or deciding
    entitlement in this project. The source’s JSA provisions at 23011–23014 differ and need separate review.\n\
    \n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 23029, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f95b98c6c9802f7ed9c7/dmg-Ch-23.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 23: Normal amount payable.\n- [DMG 23030, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e0f95b98c6c9802f7ed9c7/dmg-Ch-23.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 23: Normal amount payable.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch23`: PDF SHA-256 `174fce491e7a72ca89f2739a64ab4e2f3a0da6e33d9e48eaa5c33c7ff9a5f734`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `387302f09bbce9873dbafcd6af6a19b06842b35392e7d7771058ed22a0bd8bd2`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-applicable-amount
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes insufficient evidence for specified IS elements from the
      applicable amount as a whole.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch23/0011
      quote: "23029 When deciding an IS claim the applicable amount may be awarded without\n\n\n1. housing
        costs1 or\n\n\n2. SDP2\n\n\nif there is not enough evidence to include these elements.\n\n\n \
        \                                                                  1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 13(1);
        2 reg 13(2)"
      locator: DMG 23029
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Further information about these IS elements may support revision; the passage also
      names supersession, so this is not a mandatory single procedure.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch23/0011
      quote: "23030 The applicable amount may be revised or superseded if further information about SDP
        or housing\n\ncosts is received after the IS claim or question has been decided 1.\n\n\n     \
        \                                                                         1 SS CS (D&A) Regs,
        reg 3 & 6"
      locator: DMG 23030
  - target: term/dmg-supersession
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The same paragraph expressly names supersession as an alternative route requiring the
      decision rules to be checked.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch23/0011
      quote: "23030 The applicable amount may be revised or superseded if further information about SDP
        or housing\n\ncosts is received after the IS claim or question has been decided 1.\n\n\n     \
        \                                                                         1 SS CS (D&A) Regs,
        reg 3 & 6"
      locator: DMG 23030
